---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Delivery Methodology | Prodory" description="How Prodory delivers platform work: discovery, design as code, reviewed change, handover and a runbook your team can operate." path="/methodology/">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[900px] px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Delivery methodology</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[#4B5563]">Every engagement follows the same five stages. Each stage ends with a written artefact you keep.</p>
    <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-8">
      <li><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Discovery</h2><p class="mt-2 text-[#4B5563]">We read your current accounts, clusters and dependencies. Output: an inventory and a risk list.</p></li>
      <li><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Design as code</h2><p class="mt-2 text-[#4B5563]">The target design is written as Terraform, OpenTofu, Ansible or GitOps manifests in your repositories. Output: a reviewed design.</p></li>
      <li><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Reviewed change</h2><p class="mt-2 text-[#4B5563]">Changes arrive as pull requests with policy checks. Nothing reaches production without your review. Output: an audit trail in Git.</p></li>
      <li><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Cutover in waves</h2><p class="mt-2 text-[#4B5563]">Each wave has a rollback path that is tested before the cutover. Output: a wave report.</p></li>
      <li><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Handover</h2><p class="mt-2 text-[#4B5563]">Runbooks, a readiness checklist and a session with the team that will operate the platform. Output: a handover pack.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>
